    "narrative": "Our optimal lineup today is headlined by **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **James Wood** (71.62), both of whom leverage premium batting order positions to maximize their upside. **Mickey Moniak** is our highest-rated option due to a significant 14% park factor boost and a favorable platoon matchup that more than compensates for the SP skill of Freddy Peralta. Meanwhile, **James Wood** projects as an elite catalyst from the lead-off spot; while he loses a marginal amount of efficiency due to the opposing catcher\u2019s hold on stolen bases, his high xwOBA and prime lineup placement make him an essential anchor for our offensive floor. We are also looking for a potential ceiling game from **Brice Turang** (68.44), whose aggressive base-running environment against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him a primary target for our scarce SB category.\n\nWhile **Austin Riley** (48.23) remains in the lineup despite a tough draw against the elite Bryan Woo, the most difficult decision involved our bench. **Kyle Karros** (48.00) fell just short of a starting slot, largely because the optimizer favored the positional flexibility and higher raw efficiency of **Alex Freeland** (50.57). We also kept **Vinnie Pasquantino** (47.93) on the pine, as the massive 15% penalty against his dynamic platoon alignment neutralized any advantage he might have had against Joey Cantillo. \n\nManagers should remain alert to the \"Lineup Pending\" designations attached to **Luis Campusano**, **Josh Naylor**, **Trevor Story**, **Cole Young**, **Austin Riley**, **James Wood**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Corbin Carroll**. These placeholders, while mathematically sound based on historical trends, introduce variance; should any of these players drop in the order or sit entirely, we risk losing the \"Order\" and \"Platoon\" bonuses that currently buoy their scores. Additionally, while **Corbin Carroll** (59.08) is a start, he faces a stern test against Paul Skenes, an elite arm whose ability to suppress scoring caps the overall projection of that roster spot despite **Corbin Carroll**'s natural speed advantage.",
